{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1536344-prevent-pc-getting-too-much-fetishes","id":1536344,"title":"Prevent pc getting too much Fetishes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-05-27T05:43:35-07:00","id":1536344,"title":"Prevent pc getting too much Fetishes","content":"Let's take 2 situation: <br /> <br /> -The pc group obtain new fetishes through challenging other garou (they target those who're disrepectfull toward their fetishe and the pc's want to &quot;save&quot; them) or gain them story after story as reward for their great feats for their sept.<br /> <br /> -One of the pc know the rite to create new ones and become fetishe crafter<br /> <br /> Is there something in w20 or previous edition that prevent player to keep great amount of fetiche or do you have advices (narrative ones) to tell them they cannot just keep collecting them endlessly? I already thought about the fact that fetish aren't simple tools but actual ally deserving respect and devotion but there's enough possibility for a garou to use let's say a klaive to fight the wyrm, ape skin to hide their true nature, harmony flute to calm their packmate, mirrorshade to get through the gauntlet easily, truth earing to track traitor, chameleon skin to escape foes with silver, fang dagger for suprise attack etc... and still worship them all for each help they give him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T05:48:10-07:00","id":1536345,"title":"","content":"My personal rule is their Gnosis determines the total level<b>s</b> of fetishes you can use before the spirits start getting annoyed for being second fiddle to eachother. If someone has, say, 7 points of gnosis, I'd let them have a level 4 and a level 3 fetish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/448972/Hearthbound-Tribe-Supplement?affiliate_id=4046720\" target=\"_blank\">Hearthbound</a> and Project Director for <a href=\"https://www.tumblr.com/songoftrillium/729204622290550784/likes-dont-increase-visibility-to-others-please\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Essentials</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27167-mundusartis","name":"mundusartis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27167_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T07:34:18-07:00","id":1536355,"title":"","content":"My dear storyteller, if you wanted to deny players the chance to let their Freak Flag fly then you may have chosen the wrong setting - the World of Darkness has been kinky and Proud since the beginning!<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> Oh wait, you meant the OTHER sort of fetishes.<br /> <br /> Carry on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T08:19:02-07:00","id":1536363,"title":"","content":"This is one of those things that looks much more complicated out of play than in play. Owning fetishes is not about hoarding magical items, it's about having sacred things that require maintenance and worship. You treat them as base tools and you're going to have issues with them not co-operating when you need them or have problems when your reputations goes around.<br /> <br /> And once you've opened the gates of &quot;I'll challenge you for your loot&quot;, this makes the PC's quite targetable by the same thing by the elders - either for reclamation or punishment. This is something that I prefer to use rarely since it treads on something that's often a core part of the concept and major investment by the player, but at the end of day if their logic is &quot;I am stronger&quot;, there is always someone stronger than them, and their actions can easily be challenged and punished by a Philodox who concludes they are just being bullies.<br /> <br /> Making fetishes is so complex, involved and requires huge sacrifices from the Fetish craftsman that even elder characters will do it rarely, and if you actually play up the fact that Spirits require boons, oaths and PERMANENT gnosis to be tied into a fetish you won't see that becoming a problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T10:23:21-07:00","id":1536369,"title":"","content":"I would add that as the PCs start to hoard fetishes, if it really comes to this, they can be required to let go of some for the better of the Sept.<br /> <br /> Werewolves live at war, and those resources have to be distributed. Be it to reward a great deed or to equip a pack for a mission, when the time comes to give out fetishes it is probable the Sept will request to the well-off to provide.<br /> <br /> Give boons, renown and resources to the players when they give out their extra fetishes, and stern looks when they hoard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T14:49:11-07:00","id":1536386,"title":"","content":"I use greater Garou society to control such things. I use as a general guideline that determines who many fetishes per Garou is considered &quot;acceptable.&quot; Garou who have more than that tend to get challenged quite frequently and lose fetishes in excess of what they have. Even Garou in other septs who hear of such things will seek out those other Garou and hope to gain them. &quot;Excess&quot; fetishes tend to belong to Garou like the Sept leaders who do not use all fetishes themselves, but are willing to loan them out to favored Garou or issue them as rewards. <br /> <br /> Typically the total number of fetish levels is somewhere between zero and double their rank. If it goes beyond that, the chances of NPCs challenging and taking them increase. And sometimes it is not even a challenge needed. Sept elders can often simply decide low ranking Garou cannot be allowed to have such fetishes, or the sept starts assigning negative reknown to the &quot;selfish&quot; Garou until they give fetishes away. I treat fetishes that the Garou do not actually consider them to be private property, but belong to the Garou Nation as a whole. Individual Garou are seen only as safe guarders of them, and should a Garou seem to have too many, other Garou collectively move to make sure there is a more equal distribution. Sept leaders are somewhat exempt because their office allows them to sit on more fetishes with the proviso they can loan them out or reward other Garou as needed,<br /> <br /> The guideline is that in general Rank 1 or 2 Garou do not have any fetishes as well. That is, of course, a general rule. Some Garou do, but they tend to be one fetish no greater than their rank. Obviously, new PCs could decide to drop all five Background points or even Freebies to start with lots of fetishes. I've never seen any player do that, but it is possible. But if they want to do that, I warn them of the danger or work out other flavor text arrangements (for example, that Rank 4 klaive they'll inherit is actually kept by a trusted NPC on their behalf, but that NPC is willing to trust them with it for a particular scene). Sometimes, it's just necessary for the Garou to keep it secret how many fetishes they have.<br /> <br /> Rank 3 Garou on average with one or more fetishes equal to their level. Again, this is an average only so some Adren have less and some have more more.<br /> <br /> Rank 4 and 5 Garou typically have 1 to 4 fetishes equal to their level. Again, some Garou have less and others more.<br /> <br /> I started using this after I did a &quot;census&quot; of characters in the early Rage books to determine if there was any kind of &quot;system&quot; used in deciding what Garou had fetishes and if so, how many. This was the (non-scientific) result.<br /> <br /> I almost never have sept leaders reward rank 1 or 2 PCs with fetishes. Instead, they would given them talens. The exception being &quot;typical&quot; fetishes often granted to entire packs (but entrusting them to their pack leader). These would be &quot;common&quot; fetishes like Fangs of the Wyrm whose descriptions say they are often given to new Cliaths or packs returning from their Rite of Passage and such. <br /> <br /> That works fine for existing fetishes. But what happens when a PC learns the Rite of Fetish? While I have not seen problems in tabletop games where the ST can easily police it and make the process however time consuming and intensive as possible, I do see lots of online games where this a real problem as things quickly devolve to a matter of dice rolls and &quot;downtime&quot; which allows players to mass produce fetishes. <br /> <br /> The typical response to that is that many online STs simply require an incredibly annoying amount of dice rolls to create fetishes - extended dice rolls to research, extended dice rolls to craft, extended dice rolls to negotiate with the spirit, and so on. I think the goal is simply to exhaust the players so they only create a limited number of fetishes that they really, really want. (For talens, the thing I've seen most often is that they expire in short order, so a PC can never stockpile too many). I've never liked that because it sucks the fund out of the game. <br /> <br /> If I needed something besides making the creation of each individual fetish be a story/game in itself, I would lean to making fetish creation be a process of spending XP. Players tend to not want to waste XP, and this puts a premium on the cost of creating a fetish. Does the player really want to spend XP on something she might lose rather than something that cannot be taken away? That will eliminate a lot of over-production of fetishes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-27T15:47:54-07:00","id":1536387,"title":"","content":"Personally, I don't get too heavy handed with Fetishes, because for the most part they're not actually that powerful relative to the cost of getting them (and ease of losing them). Since it's more of a tone/flavor setting issue than anything else... run the setting to reflect how you want things to be. Garou outright owning individual Fetishes is supposed to be rare-ish, and most Fetishes are supposed to be held communally by the Sept for Sept leadership to assign as needed, with the expectation of their return once a task is complete.<br /> <br /> That said, Tribes that highly value PB are more likely to let high PB members be exceptions (esp. if a Fetish is a family heirloom), and on the opposite side of things, some Glass Walker and Bone Gnawer Fetishes might end up &quot;stockpiled&quot; by a single character because none of the other Tribes actually want them to contest over them.<br /> <br /> I actually find the game to work better when most Garou have a Fetish or two, but have to actually take care of the spirits in them, because it helps highlight the individual animism of each character rather than the way spirits and Garou interact be more abstract or formal. I even once did a whole set of house rules to make Fetishes more like Relics from Scion (with a significant change to how Gifts are accessed to make with Scion's approach to powers), and it did feel like it stressed the animism of the game a lot more to have a constant personal spirit relationship to maintain. But that's not how the setting is described.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T17:32:58-07:00","id":1536473,"title":"","content":"The relationship between fetiche and garou is not something well detailed in w20 core book, i understood it must be similar to have an ally you call for help rather than tool.<br /> <br /> That fact alone is preventing my pc to try and collect a way or another fetiche, so i didn't actually had the issue, but sometimes when writting the next story i just feel that i miss somthing with fetiche, that i should try making a thing with them, more interesting than just set unworthy garou direspect those they use and let pc choose to intervene or not.<br /> <br /> Same for fetiche rite, giving extended roll is boring, and take too much time to run a full story is too much, without even talking about the lack of advice from the boon to create original one, so we feel it could be great to play and a good part of the story but when it come to apply it, motivation fail us","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-28T20:52:01-07:00","id":1536479,"title":"","content":"I think you're focusing too much on the wrong method.<br /> <br /> Garou that disrespect their fetishes shouldn't be all that common, and PCs looking for them as a means to get fetishes wouldn't find more than one or two for an entire chronicle. Not one or two per PC, but one or two total.<br /> <br /> Most fetishes a Garou get are rewards for their feats in service of the Sept, usually items that belonged to many others before, or a family heirloom they, again, have to work hard to prove they deserve it.<br /> <br /> The other staple on getting fetishes is to find lost fetishes. Many such items get lost when their users die in action or lose them in other ways. They end up in museums, private collections, enemy hands, or in the depts of the Umbra. The quest to recover a lost fetish is itself a honorable one, but even during other missions a pack may find something and claim it for themselves.<br /> <br /> Even the crafting of a fetish should be a whole story in itself not because it is a powerful resource, but because it is a big feat as it increases the limited arsenal of the Sept, even if at first it remains with the pack. Crafting a fetish is a source of renown with good reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}